# GOD BLESS AMERICA – Traditional/Kate Smith
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
{ns}
{define: CaddG base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 1 3} 
{define: D4 base-fret 1 frets x x 0 2 3 3}
{define: Gadd base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 3 3} 
{t: GOD BLESS AMERICA – Traditional/Kate Smith }
{st: (Berlin) }
{artist: Kate Smith }
{composer: Irving Berlin  }


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6pZ1brENIjw&t=76s  (Capo 5)

TIP:  This version adds a reprise like Kate Smith did when she sang it before the Philadelphia Flyers home games.  (Had she still been around for the 1997 Stanley Cup Finals perhaps they wouldn't have been humiliatingly swept by the Detroit Red Wings.)  The first time around the inflection is down on “home” and on the second “home” it’s up.  And of course the finale is up.   

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) and (CaddG) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  (D4) only appears in the intro and is just (D) with your pinky added to the 1st string/3rd fret.  (Dsus2) is just (D) without the middle finger and it always follows a (D) so just lift off/on like a toggle.  (Cmaj7) is (C) without the index finger and (CaddG) is (C) with pinky on the 1st string/3rd fret.  
      

[INTRO:]     [G]     [C]     [D]     [D4]       [D]     [(pause)]


[G]God [D]bless [Dsus2]A      [D]mer [Dsus2]I      [D]ca, [D7]land that I [G]love.
Stand be[C]side her, and [G]guide her, through the night with a [D]light from [G]above.


From the [D]mountains, to the [G]prairies, to the [C]oceans, [Cmaj7]white [C]with [Gadd]foam.  
[C]God [G]bless [C]A[G]merica, [C]my [G]home, [D]sweet [G]home.


From the [D]mountains, to the [G]prairies, to the [C]oceans, [Cmaj7]white [C]with [Gadd]foam. 
[C]God [G]bless [C]A [G]merica, [C]my [G]home, [D]sweet [Gadd]home.


